"<p>SaaSBase supports multi-cloud storage destinations for backups. Storing backups off-server ensures that you can recover your entire infrastructure even if a physical server is lost.</p>\n<h2>Supported Providers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cloudflare R2:</strong> Zero egress fees (Highly recommended).</li>\n<li><strong>Amazon S3:</strong> Standard AWS object storage.</li>\n<li><strong>Backblaze B2:</strong> Cost-effective S3-compatible cloud storage.</li>\n<li><strong>Local Server Folder:</strong> Stored on the local host filesystem for quick rollback.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Adding a Destination</h2>\n<p>Navigate to <strong>Data -> Destinations -> Add Destination</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> S3 Compatible</li>\n<li><strong>Bucket Name:</strong> e.g. <code>my-saasbase-backups</code></li>\n<li><strong>Endpoint:</strong> e.g. <code>https://&#x3C;account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com</code></li>\n<li><strong>Access Key ID &#x26; Secret Access Key</strong> (Encrypted at rest using HKDF).</li>\n</ul>"